THOUGHT: Marking primitiveTypeOf as @Nullable fixed the original RETURN_NULLABLE error but exposed new call-site errors where its nullable result is dereferenced or passed to a @NonNull parameter. I need to adjust isAssignableFromWrapper to handle the nullable return safely, preserving behavior. Since isPrimitiveOrWrapper ensures both arguments are primitive or wrapper, primitiveTypeOf should never return null in that branch; I can use local variables, assert non-null via Objects.requireNonNull, and keep NullAway satisfied without changing semantics. Then I’ll re-run the build to confirm the Primitives-related errors are gone and no new ones appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/mockito && sed -i '42,52c\  public static boolean isPrimitiveOrWrapper(Class<?> type) {
    return PRIMITIVE_OR_WRAPPER_DEFAULT_VALUES.containsKey(type);
  }

  public static boolean isAssignableFromWrapper(Class<?> valueClass, Class<?> referenceType) {
    if (isPrimitiveOrWrapper(valueClass) && isPrimitiveOrWrapper(referenceType)) {
      Class<?> valuePrimitive = primitiveTypeOf(valueClass);
      Class<?> referencePrimitive = primitiveTypeOf(referenceType);
      if (valuePrimitive == null || referencePrimitive == null) {
        return false;
      }
      return valuePrimitive.isAssignableFrom(referencePrimitive);
    }
    return false;
  }' src/main/java/org/mockito/internal/util/Primitives.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "Primitives.java" new_build_output.log || true && tail -n 5 new_build_output.log
```

